codemap 9
tour io-config
kind layer
author ai
group gui
note The io-config crate: the user's own files in the codemap config folder, the saved panel layout and the settings, each a small text file per user. user_file is the one lookup: the file's variable (CODEMAP_LAYOUT, CODEMAP_SETTINGS) when set, else codemap/<name> under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME, ~/.config or %APPDATA%; a script or screenshot run asks with Reach::OverrideOnly, so only the variable reaches it and a run never reads or writes the user's real files. LayoutStore and SettingsStore each have find, load and save: load gives None for a missing or unreadable file and the GUI starts from its defaults, save creates the folder and writes through io-store. The layout is rejected whole when any line is wrong; the settings keep every line that reads and drop the others, since one typo should not cost the rest. The values are domain's LayoutTree, which knows view names only as ViewKeys, and Settings.

